%Immediate: the condition of Definition~\ref{def:realisable} is universally quantified over the zone, and
%$Z'$ is a non-empty subset of $Z$.
%\end{proof}
%
%Lemma~\ref{lem:narrowing} is what licenses the refinement rule \ruleref{Covstar} to be a disjunctive
%choice rather than a case analysis: a node is free to commit to a tighter entry constraint. For this to
%be sound at the level of the extracted automaton, the narrowing must happen \emph{before} the node's
%outgoing steps are fixed; this is guaranteed by the discipline of \S\ref{ss:rules}, where a node is
%saturated and covered to exhaustion before any successor is generated, so the guards of its delays and
%edges are read off the narrowed zone.

\noindent
The construction branches two ways. An \emph{OR} (disjunctive, $\ORn$) node is realisable if
\emph{some} child is; an \emph{AND} (conjunctive, $\ANDn$) node requires \emph{all} its children. Some
rules are deterministic ($\DETn$): a single child, replacing the node. 


